@page "/docs/primitives/autocomplete"

<DocsPage Title="Autocomplete" Description="An input that suggests options as you type.">
    <ComponentPreview Name="primitives/autocomplete-hero" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Usage guidelines" />
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Avoid when selection state is needed:</strong> Use <a href="/docs/primitives/combobox">Combobox</a> instead of Autocomplete if the selection should be remembered and the input can't hold custom text. Unlike Combobox, Autocomplete's input can contain free-form text, as its suggestions only <em>optionally</em> complete the text.</li>
        <li><strong>Form controls must have an accessible name:</strong> Give it one with a <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> element or the <a href="/docs/primitives/field">Field</a> parts.</li>
        <li><strong>Closing animations:</strong> The popup stays rendered until its closing animation finishes. See <a href="/docs/primitives/animation">Animation</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <DocsHeading Title="Anatomy" />
    <p>Import the primitives and assemble the parts:</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@Anatomy" />
